{"content":[{"c":["CLOPAS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Husband of Mary, one of the women who was present at Jesus’ crucifixion (",{"href":"?bref=John.19.25","r":"John.19.25","rawR":"John.19.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.19.25","value":"John.19.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 19:25"},"). From the Greek it cannot be determined if Mary the wife of Clopas was also the sister of Jesus’ mother or a different person. One tradition identifies Clopas as the brother of Joseph. Another links him with Cleopas of ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.24.18","r":"Luke.24.18","rawR":"Luke.24.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.24.18","value":"Luke.24.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 24:18"},", even though “Clopas” is of Hebrew origin and “Cleopas” is Greek. A third possibility is to equate him with Alphaeus. This is feasible only if James, son of Alphaeus (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.10.3","r":"Matt.10.3","rawR":"Matt.10.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.10.3","value":"Matt.10.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 10:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.6.15","r":"Luke.6.15","rawR":"Luke.6.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.6.15","value":"Luke.6.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 6:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.1.13","r":"Acts.1.13","rawR":"Acts.1.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.1.13","value":"Acts.1.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 1:13"},") is the same as James, son of Mary (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.56","r":"Matt.27.56","rawR":"Matt.27.56","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.56","value":"Matt.27.56"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:56"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.15.40","r":"Mark.15.40","rawR":"Mark.15.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.15.40","value":"Mark.15.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 15:40"},"), and Mary is the same person mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=John.19.25","r":"John.19.25","rawR":"John.19.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.19.25","value":"John.19.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 19:25"},". These suggestions are theoretical; it is possible that Clopas, Cleopas, and Alphaeus are all separate individuals."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Clopas","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jn 19:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.19.25","rawQueryValue":"John.19.25","sourceRefExact":"John.19.25"},{"anchorText":"Luke 24:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.24.18","rawQueryValue":"Luke.24.18","sourceRefExact":"Luke.24.18"},{"anchorText":"Mt 10:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.10.3","rawQueryValue":"Matt.10.3","sourceRefExact":"Matt.10.3"},{"anchorText":"Lk 6:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.6.15","rawQueryValue":"Luke.6.15","sourceRefExact":"Luke.6.15"},{"anchorText":"Acts 1:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.1.13","rawQueryValue":"Acts.1.13","sourceRefExact":"Acts.1.13"},{"anchorText":"Mt 27:56","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.56","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.56","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.56"},{"anchorText":"Mk 15:40","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.15.40","rawQueryValue":"Mark.15.40","sourceRefExact":"Mark.15.40"},{"anchorText":"John 19:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.19.25","rawQueryValue":"John.19.25","sourceRefExact":"John.19.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"94a8daf7612804cfb53f68a5890ee3c691815d2aabbd4568e093bd2ac2d5bcd1","sourceItemName":"Clopas","sourceItemOrder":223,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Clopas","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Clopas","title":"Clopas","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}